{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## SCOPE STOP: this is not a mechanical wrong-return-type defect — no patch attempted\n\nA `/rebar-debug` pass was dispatched against this ticket **scoped as a mechanical defect** (\"the verifier\nreturns the wrong record type; fix the type/wiring so it returns a `CompletionVerdict`; do not redesign the\ncompletion-verification contract and do not change verification behavior beyond correcting the returned\nrecord\"). That scope does not fit the defect. Stopping in Phase 1 without writing code, and recording why.\n\n### Independent replication of the recorded root cause (not a relay of the earlier comment)\n\nVerified every citation in the ROOT CAUSE comment against the working tree at `origin/main` c3fb869ab5, then\nreproduced the failure deterministically and locally:\n\n```python\nCV = contracts.completion_verdict_response_model()\nreply = \"...prose... ```json {\\\"relation\\\":\\\"depends_on\\\",\\\"target_id\\\":\\\"f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31\\\"} ``` ...\n         Final verdict: ```json {\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"criteria\\\":[],\\\"summary\\\":\\\"all met\\\"} ```\"\nstructured.parse_structured(reply, CV)\n```\n\nfails with the reported error **verbatim**, including pydantic's middle-truncated render:\n\n```\nstructured output failed validation: 1 validation error for CompletionVerdict\nverdict\n  Field required [type=missing, input_value={'relation': 'depends_on'...: 'f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31'}, input_type=dict]\n```\n\n`structured.tolerant_parse(reply, schema=CV)` returns `{'relation': 'depends_on', 'target_id': 'f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31'}` —\nthe `Dep`, not the verdict. Control: the identical reply with the quoted dep record removed parses to\n`verdict='PASS' findings=[] criteria=[] summary='all met'`. So the model's verdict is present and valid; only\nthe **selection** is wrong. Confirms the RCA and re-refutes \"model formatting drift\".\n\nCitations re-verified as accurate on current `main`:\n`llm/structured.py:138-140` (`_FENCE_RE.search` — first fence wins), `:82-118` + `:146-150`\n(`_first_json_object` — first *parseable* object wins, `model_cls` never consulted),\n`:199` (`parse_structured` = `validate_to(model_cls, tolerant_parse(text, schema=model_cls))` — the schema\nreaches json-repair only), `llm/capabilities.py:273-275` (`_is_claude -> native_structured_output: False`),\n`llm/structured_run.py:201` (`Agent(model, **kwargs)`, `output_type` defaults to `str`) and `:213`,\n`llm/pai_tools.py:219-232` (`show_ticket` returns raw ticket JSON incl. `deps`), `types.py:52-57` (`Dep`).\n\n### Why the mechanical scope does not apply\n\nNothing returns the wrong type. The verifier's wiring is correct and correctly typed: `parse_structured` is\ncalled with `CompletionVerdict` and *does* validate against it. There is no type annotation, no `return`, and\nno call site to correct. The defect is a **selection policy** — `tolerant_parse` picks the first JSON object\nthat *parses* rather than the first that *satisfies* `model_cls` — and that policy is:\n\n* **deliberate and documented**, not an oversight: `_first_json_object`'s docstring states first-wins exists so\n  \"a model that emits a draft then a correction does not get the last-wins surprise json-repair gives\" (bug\n  67ee / messianic-wild-dassie);\n* **shared by every structured LLM call in rebar** — plan-review, ticket-digest, overlap, epic-bug-screen — so\n  changing it changes verification behavior well beyond the completion verifier. This ticket's own E3\n  experiment found the key-overlap screen load-bearing precisely because the all-defaults contracts\n  (`OverlapVerdict`, `TicketDigest`, `EpicBugScreenVerdict`) validate `{}` and would degenerate to\n  trailing-junk/empty-object wins under a naive schema filter;\n* **not correctable at the extractor alone** — E2 recorded that the directive at `structured.py:76-79` (\"no\n  prose, no markdown fence\") and the extraction change must ship **atomically**, because a model that *obeys*\n  the current directive makes the failure *more* likely.\n\nAny real fix therefore changes a documented contract and verification behavior across callers. That is the\ndesign decision the dispatch scope explicitly excluded, so no code was written and no claim was taken.\n\n### Recommended disposition\n\nThe ticket is already past debugging: root cause proven, four derisking experiments (E1-E4, 39 live Bedrock\ncalls) complete, and a converged multi-layer fix architecture recorded, with the next step noted as \"plan into\ndescription\". It needs the **plan + decomposition + plan-review** path, not another debug pass. Re-dispatching\nthis as a mechanical fix will keep hitting this same stop.\n\nAlso unchanged: `b586-2fda-8a15-4260` stays `in_progress`; do not `--force-close` it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785891773804050001,"uuid":"a0043419-42ad-48af-9dcc-ab8a767c2a16"}